{
  "book": "alma",
  "bookName": "Alma",
  "chapter": 42,
  "voice": {
    "provider": "elevenlabs",
    "voice_id": "ddDFRErfhdc2asyySOG5",
    "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2",
    "settings": {
      "stability": 0.5,
      "similarity_boost": 0.75,
      "style": 0.35,
      "use_speaker_boost": true
    },
    "name": "Samuel"
  },
  "pauses": {
    "line_ms": 180,
    "verse_ms": 500
  },
  "duration": 457.996,
  "lines": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.019,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, my son, I perceive there is somewhat more",
      "verse": "42:1",
      "lineIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 3.199,
      "end": 5.01,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which doth worry your mind,",
      "verse": "42:1",
      "lineIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 5.19,
      "end": 6.862,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which ye cannot understand\u2014",
      "verse": "42:1",
      "lineIndex": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 7.042,
      "end": 11.872,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which is concerning the justice of God in the punishment of the sinner;",
      "verse": "42:1",
      "lineIndex": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 12.052,
      "end": 14.885,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "for ye do try to suppose that it is injustice",
      "verse": "42:1",
      "lineIndex": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 15.065,
      "end": 18.502,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that the sinner should be consigned to a state of misery.",
      "verse": "42:1",
      "lineIndex": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 19.182,
      "end": 20.715,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now behold, my son,",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 20.895,
      "end": 22.892,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "I will explain this thing unto thee.",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 8
    },
    {
      "start": 23.072,
      "end": 28.923,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "For behold, after the Lord God sent our first parents forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground,",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 9
    },
    {
      "start": 29.103,
      "end": 32.4,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "from whence they were taken\u2014yea, he drew out the man,",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 10
    },
    {
      "start": 32.58,
      "end": 36.342,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and he placed at the east end of the garden of Eden, cherubim,",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 11
    },
    {
      "start": 36.522,
      "end": 38.937,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and a flaming sword which turned every way,",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 12
    },
    {
      "start": 39.117,
      "end": 40.789,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "to keep the tree of life\u2014",
      "verse": "42:2",
      "lineIndex": 13
    },
    {
      "start": 41.469,
      "end": 46.485,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now, we see that the man had become as God, knowing good and evil;",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 14
    },
    {
      "start": 46.665,
      "end": 49.126,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and lest he should put forth his hand,",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 15
    },
    {
      "start": 49.306,
      "end": 51.814,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and take also of the tree of life,",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 16
    },
    {
      "start": 51.994,
      "end": 53.062,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and eat",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 17
    },
    {
      "start": 53.242,
      "end": 54.775,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and live forever,",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 18
    },
    {
      "start": 54.955,
      "end": 58.113,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "the Lord God placed cherubim and the flaming sword,",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 19
    },
    {
      "start": 58.293,
      "end": 60.569,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that he should not partake of the fruit\u2014",
      "verse": "42:3",
      "lineIndex": 20
    },
    {
      "start": 61.249,
      "end": 66.265,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And thus we see, that there was a time granted unto man to repent,",
      "verse": "42:4",
      "lineIndex": 21
    },
    {
      "start": 66.445,
      "end": 70.207,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "yea, a probationary time, a time to repent and serve God.",
      "verse": "42:4",
      "lineIndex": 22
    },
    {
      "start": 70.887,
      "end": 74.324,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "For behold, if Adam had put forth his hand immediately,",
      "verse": "42:5",
      "lineIndex": 23
    },
    {
      "start": 74.504,
      "end": 76.919,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and partaken of the tree of life,",
      "verse": "42:5",
      "lineIndex": 24
    },
    {
      "start": 77.099,
      "end": 83.461,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "he would have lived forever, according to the word of God, having no space for repentance;",
      "verse": "42:5",
      "lineIndex": 25
    },
    {
      "start": 83.641,
      "end": 86.752,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "yea, and also the word of God would have been void,",
      "verse": "42:5",
      "lineIndex": 26
    },
    {
      "start": 86.932,
      "end": 90.229,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and the great plan of salvation would have been frustrated.",
      "verse": "42:5",
      "lineIndex": 27
    },
    {
      "start": 90.909,
      "end": 93.881,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "But behold, it was appointed unto man to die\u2014",
      "verse": "42:6",
      "lineIndex": 28
    },
    {
      "start": 94.061,
      "end": 97.59,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore, as they were cut off from the tree of life",
      "verse": "42:6",
      "lineIndex": 29
    },
    {
      "start": 97.77,
      "end": 104.132,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "they should be cut off from the face of the earth\u2014 and man became lost forever,",
      "verse": "42:6",
      "lineIndex": 30
    },
    {
      "start": 104.312,
      "end": 106.077,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "yea, they became fallen man.",
      "verse": "42:6",
      "lineIndex": 31
    },
    {
      "start": 106.757,
      "end": 110.797,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, ye see by this that our first parents were cut off",
      "verse": "42:7",
      "lineIndex": 32
    },
    {
      "start": 110.977,
      "end": 115.667,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "both temporally and spiritually from the presence of the Lord;",
      "verse": "42:7",
      "lineIndex": 33
    },
    {
      "start": 115.847,
      "end": 119.934,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and thus we see they became subjects to follow after their own will.",
      "verse": "42:7",
      "lineIndex": 34
    },
    {
      "start": 120.614,
      "end": 125.908,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now behold, it was not expedient that man should be reclaimed from this temporal death,",
      "verse": "42:8",
      "lineIndex": 35
    },
    {
      "start": 126.088,
      "end": 129.153,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "for that would destroy the great plan of happiness.",
      "verse": "42:8",
      "lineIndex": 36
    },
    {
      "start": 129.833,
      "end": 132.759,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Therefore, as the soul could never die,",
      "verse": "42:9",
      "lineIndex": 37
    },
    {
      "start": 132.939,
      "end": 138.698,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and the fall had brought upon all mankind a spiritual death as well as a temporal,",
      "verse": "42:9",
      "lineIndex": 38
    },
    {
      "start": 138.878,
      "end": 146.308,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that is, they were cut off from the presence of the Lord, it was expedient that mankind should be reclaimed from this spiritual death.",
      "verse": "42:9",
      "lineIndex": 39
    },
    {
      "start": 146.988,
      "end": 150.564,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Therefore, as they had become carnal, sensual,",
      "verse": "42:10",
      "lineIndex": 41
    },
    {
      "start": 150.744,
      "end": 152.416,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and devilish, by nature,",
      "verse": "42:10",
      "lineIndex": 42
    },
    {
      "start": 152.596,
      "end": 156.265,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "this probationary state became a state for them to prepare;",
      "verse": "42:10",
      "lineIndex": 43
    },
    {
      "start": 156.445,
      "end": 158.535,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "it became a preparatory state.",
      "verse": "42:10",
      "lineIndex": 44
    },
    {
      "start": 159.215,
      "end": 161.073,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now remember, my son,",
      "verse": "42:11",
      "lineIndex": 45
    },
    {
      "start": 161.253,
      "end": 165.2,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "if it were not for the plan of redemption, (laying it aside)",
      "verse": "42:11",
      "lineIndex": 46
    },
    {
      "start": 165.38,
      "end": 170.442,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "as soon as they were dead their souls were miserable, being cut off from the presence of the Lord.",
      "verse": "42:11",
      "lineIndex": 47
    },
    {
      "start": 171.122,
      "end": 174.884,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, there was no means to reclaim men from this fallen state,",
      "verse": "42:12",
      "lineIndex": 48
    },
    {
      "start": 175.064,
      "end": 179.429,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which man had brought upon himself because of his own disobedience;",
      "verse": "42:12",
      "lineIndex": 49
    },
    {
      "start": 180.109,
      "end": 182.199,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Therefore, according to justice,",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 50
    },
    {
      "start": 182.379,
      "end": 185.305,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "the plan of redemption could not be brought about,",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 51
    },
    {
      "start": 185.485,
      "end": 189.804,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "only on conditions of repentance of men in this probationary state,",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 52
    },
    {
      "start": 189.984,
      "end": 191.934,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "yea, this preparatory state;",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 53
    },
    {
      "start": 192.114,
      "end": 194.9,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "for except it were for these conditions,",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 54
    },
    {
      "start": 195.08,
      "end": 200.096,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "mercy could not take effect except it should destroy the work of justice.",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 55
    },
    {
      "start": 200.276,
      "end": 203.062,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now the work of justice could not be destroyed;",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 56
    },
    {
      "start": 203.242,
      "end": 205.657,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "if so, God would cease to be God.",
      "verse": "42:13",
      "lineIndex": 57
    },
    {
      "start": 206.337,
      "end": 209.123,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And thus we see that all mankind were fallen,",
      "verse": "42:14",
      "lineIndex": 58
    },
    {
      "start": 209.303,
      "end": 211.857,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and they were in the grasp of justice;",
      "verse": "42:14",
      "lineIndex": 59
    },
    {
      "start": 212.037,
      "end": 216.913,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "yea, the justice of God, which consigned them forever to be cut off from his presence.",
      "verse": "42:14",
      "lineIndex": 60
    },
    {
      "start": 217.593,
      "end": 220.287,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, the plan of mercy could not be brought about",
      "verse": "42:15",
      "lineIndex": 62
    },
    {
      "start": 220.467,
      "end": 222.789,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "except an atonement should be made;",
      "verse": "42:15",
      "lineIndex": 63
    },
    {
      "start": 222.969,
      "end": 228.356,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "therefore God himself atoneth for the sins of the world, to bring about the plan of mercy,",
      "verse": "42:15",
      "lineIndex": 64
    },
    {
      "start": 228.536,
      "end": 230.858,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "to appease the demands of justice,",
      "verse": "42:15",
      "lineIndex": 65
    },
    {
      "start": 231.038,
      "end": 233.685,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that God might be a perfect, just God,",
      "verse": "42:15",
      "lineIndex": 66
    },
    {
      "start": 233.865,
      "end": 235.769,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and a merciful God also.",
      "verse": "42:15",
      "lineIndex": 67
    },
    {
      "start": 236.449,
      "end": 238.957,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now, repentance could not come unto men",
      "verse": "42:16",
      "lineIndex": 68
    },
    {
      "start": 239.137,
      "end": 241.32,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "except there were a punishment,",
      "verse": "42:16",
      "lineIndex": 69
    },
    {
      "start": 241.5,
      "end": 244.565,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which also was eternal as the life of the soul",
      "verse": "42:16",
      "lineIndex": 70
    },
    {
      "start": 244.745,
      "end": 248.228,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "should be, affixed opposite to the plan of happiness,",
      "verse": "42:16",
      "lineIndex": 71
    },
    {
      "start": 248.408,
      "end": 251.752,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which was as eternal also as the life of the soul.",
      "verse": "42:16",
      "lineIndex": 72
    },
    {
      "start": 252.432,
      "end": 255.265,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now, how could a man repent except he should sin?",
      "verse": "42:17",
      "lineIndex": 73
    },
    {
      "start": 255.445,
      "end": 257.674,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "How could he sin if there was no law?",
      "verse": "42:17",
      "lineIndex": 74
    },
    {
      "start": 257.854,
      "end": 261.383,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "How could there be a law save there was a punishment?",
      "verse": "42:17",
      "lineIndex": 75
    },
    {
      "start": 262.063,
      "end": 264.571,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now, there was a punishment affixed,",
      "verse": "42:18",
      "lineIndex": 76
    },
    {
      "start": 264.751,
      "end": 266.516,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and a just law given,",
      "verse": "42:18",
      "lineIndex": 77
    },
    {
      "start": 266.696,
      "end": 269.575,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which brought remorse of conscience unto man.",
      "verse": "42:18",
      "lineIndex": 78
    },
    {
      "start": 270.255,
      "end": 274.342,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Now, if there was no law given\u2014if a man murdered he should die\u2014",
      "verse": "42:19",
      "lineIndex": 79
    },
    {
      "start": 274.522,
      "end": 277.401,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "would he be afraid he would die if he should murder?",
      "verse": "42:19",
      "lineIndex": 80
    },
    {
      "start": 278.081,
      "end": 281.61,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And also, if there was no law given against sin",
      "verse": "42:20",
      "lineIndex": 81
    },
    {
      "start": 281.79,
      "end": 284.112,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "men would not be afraid to sin.",
      "verse": "42:20",
      "lineIndex": 82
    },
    {
      "start": 284.792,
      "end": 287.903,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And if there was no law given, if men sinned",
      "verse": "42:21",
      "lineIndex": 83
    },
    {
      "start": 288.083,
      "end": 290.591,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "what could justice do, or mercy either,",
      "verse": "42:21",
      "lineIndex": 84
    },
    {
      "start": 290.771,
      "end": 293.139,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "for they would have no claim upon the creature?",
      "verse": "42:21",
      "lineIndex": 85
    },
    {
      "start": 293.819,
      "end": 299.531,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "But there is a law given, and a punishment affixed, and a repentance granted;",
      "verse": "42:22",
      "lineIndex": 86
    },
    {
      "start": 299.711,
      "end": 302.126,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which repentance, mercy claimeth;",
      "verse": "42:22",
      "lineIndex": 87
    },
    {
      "start": 302.306,
      "end": 306.718,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "otherwise, justice claimeth the creature and executeth the law,",
      "verse": "42:22",
      "lineIndex": 88
    },
    {
      "start": 306.898,
      "end": 309.359,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and the law inflicteth the punishment;",
      "verse": "42:22",
      "lineIndex": 89
    },
    {
      "start": 309.539,
      "end": 312.743,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "if not so, the works of justice would be destroyed,",
      "verse": "42:22",
      "lineIndex": 90
    },
    {
      "start": 312.923,
      "end": 314.966,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and God would cease to be God.",
      "verse": "42:22",
      "lineIndex": 91
    },
    {
      "start": 315.646,
      "end": 317.736,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "But God ceaseth not to be God,",
      "verse": "42:23",
      "lineIndex": 92
    },
    {
      "start": 317.916,
      "end": 320.145,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and mercy claimeth the penitent,",
      "verse": "42:23",
      "lineIndex": 93
    },
    {
      "start": 320.325,
      "end": 322.74,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and mercy cometh because of the atonement;",
      "verse": "42:23",
      "lineIndex": 94
    },
    {
      "start": 322.92,
      "end": 326.96,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and the atonement bringeth to pass the resurrection of the dead;",
      "verse": "42:23",
      "lineIndex": 95
    },
    {
      "start": 327.14,
      "end": 332.063,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and the resurrection of the dead bringeth back men into the presence of God;",
      "verse": "42:23",
      "lineIndex": 96
    },
    {
      "start": 332.243,
      "end": 339.813,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and thus they are restored into his presence, to be judged according to their works, according to the law and justice.",
      "verse": "42:23",
      "lineIndex": 97
    },
    {
      "start": 340.493,
      "end": 343.651,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "For behold, justice exerciseth all his demands,",
      "verse": "42:24",
      "lineIndex": 99
    },
    {
      "start": 343.831,
      "end": 346.942,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and also mercy claimeth all which is her own;",
      "verse": "42:24",
      "lineIndex": 100
    },
    {
      "start": 347.122,
      "end": 350.559,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and thus, none but the truly penitent are saved.",
      "verse": "42:24",
      "lineIndex": 101
    },
    {
      "start": 351.239,
      "end": 353.979,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "What, do ye suppose that mercy can rob justice?",
      "verse": "42:25",
      "lineIndex": 102
    },
    {
      "start": 354.159,
      "end": 355.645,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "I say unto you,",
      "verse": "42:25",
      "lineIndex": 103
    },
    {
      "start": 355.825,
      "end": 357.125,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Nay; not one whit.",
      "verse": "42:25",
      "lineIndex": 104
    },
    {
      "start": 357.305,
      "end": 359.534,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "If so, God would cease to be God.",
      "verse": "42:25",
      "lineIndex": 105
    },
    {
      "start": 360.214,
      "end": 364.208,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And thus God bringeth about his great and eternal purposes,",
      "verse": "42:26",
      "lineIndex": 106
    },
    {
      "start": 364.388,
      "end": 368.66,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which were prepared from the foundation of the world.",
      "verse": "42:26",
      "lineIndex": 107
    },
    {
      "start": 368.84,
      "end": 375.527,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And thus cometh about the salvation and the redemption of men, and also their destruction and misery.",
      "verse": "42:26",
      "lineIndex": 108
    },
    {
      "start": 376.207,
      "end": 378.808,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Therefore, O my son, whosoever will come",
      "verse": "42:27",
      "lineIndex": 110
    },
    {
      "start": 378.988,
      "end": 382.378,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "may come and partake of the waters of life freely;",
      "verse": "42:27",
      "lineIndex": 111
    },
    {
      "start": 382.558,
      "end": 384.369,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and whosoever will not come",
      "verse": "42:27",
      "lineIndex": 112
    },
    {
      "start": 384.549,
      "end": 386.592,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "the same is not compelled to come;",
      "verse": "42:27",
      "lineIndex": 113
    },
    {
      "start": 386.772,
      "end": 391.788,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "but in the last day it shall be restored unto him according to his deeds.",
      "verse": "42:27",
      "lineIndex": 114
    },
    {
      "start": 392.468,
      "end": 394.604,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "If he has desired to do evil,",
      "verse": "42:28",
      "lineIndex": 115
    },
    {
      "start": 394.784,
      "end": 397.013,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and has not repented in his days,",
      "verse": "42:28",
      "lineIndex": 116
    },
    {
      "start": 397.193,
      "end": 401.373,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "behold, evil shall be done unto him, according to the restoration of God.",
      "verse": "42:28",
      "lineIndex": 117
    },
    {
      "start": 402.053,
      "end": 403.446,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, my son,",
      "verse": "42:29",
      "lineIndex": 118
    },
    {
      "start": 403.626,
      "end": 406.97,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "I desire that ye should let these things trouble you no more,",
      "verse": "42:29",
      "lineIndex": 119
    },
    {
      "start": 407.15,
      "end": 410.308,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and only let your sins trouble you, with that trouble",
      "verse": "42:29",
      "lineIndex": 120
    },
    {
      "start": 410.488,
      "end": 413.182,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "which shall bring you down unto repentance.",
      "verse": "42:29",
      "lineIndex": 121
    },
    {
      "start": 413.862,
      "end": 414.977,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "O my son,",
      "verse": "42:30",
      "lineIndex": 122
    },
    {
      "start": 415.157,
      "end": 418.501,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "I desire that ye should deny the justice of God no more.",
      "verse": "42:30",
      "lineIndex": 123
    },
    {
      "start": 418.681,
      "end": 425.229,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Do not endeavor to excuse yourself in the least point because of your sins, by denying the justice of God;",
      "verse": "42:30",
      "lineIndex": 124
    },
    {
      "start": 425.409,
      "end": 428.52,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "but do you let the justice of God, and his mercy,",
      "verse": "42:30",
      "lineIndex": 125
    },
    {
      "start": 428.7,
      "end": 431.951,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and his long-suffering have full sway in your heart;",
      "verse": "42:30",
      "lineIndex": 126
    },
    {
      "start": 432.131,
      "end": 434.964,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "and let it bring you down to the dust in humility.",
      "verse": "42:30",
      "lineIndex": 127
    },
    {
      "start": 435.644,
      "end": 437.177,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, O my son,",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 128
    },
    {
      "start": 437.357,
      "end": 440.84,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "ye are called of God to preach the word unto this people.",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 129
    },
    {
      "start": 441.02,
      "end": 443.017,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And now, my son, go thy way,",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 130
    },
    {
      "start": 443.197,
      "end": 446.169,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "declare the word with truth and soberness,",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 131
    },
    {
      "start": 446.349,
      "end": 449.646,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that thou mayest bring souls unto repentance,",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 132
    },
    {
      "start": 449.826,
      "end": 453.077,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "that the great plan of mercy may have claim upon them.",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 133
    },
    {
      "start": 453.257,
      "end": 456.322,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "And may God grant unto you even according to my words.",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 134
    },
    {
      "start": 456.502,
      "end": 457.338,
      "type": "line",
      "text": "Amen.",
      "verse": "42:31",
      "lineIndex": 135
    }
  ]
}